<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dharmapala of Kotte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1541–1597</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Dom João Dharmapala</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dharmapala of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-jayawardenepura-kotte">Kotte</a> was the last king of Kotte in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, placed on the throne as a child in 1551 under Portuguese protection. Baptised as Dom João Dharmapala in 1557, he lost the support of most of his subjects to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayadunne">Mayadunne</a> of Sitawaka. In 1580 he bequeathed his kingdom to the King of Portugal, and it passed to Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a> on his death in 1597.</p></div>
